    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nForkin Earls Property are delighted to present this impressive and spacious detached residence extending to approximately 225.9 sq. m. And set on approx. 0.5-acre site in the picturesque village of Glenealy, Co. Wicklow. Nestled in a beautiful countryside setting, the property enjoys views of Carrig Mountain to the front and rolling countryside views to the rear, offering the perfect balance of rural tranquillity and convenience.\n\nThe property is approached through attractive brick entrance pillars with wooden gates, opening onto a sweeping gravel driveway that provides ample parking and creates a welcoming approach to the house. The house is surrounded by beautifully maintained gardens to the front and rear, mainly laid in lawn and bordered by mature hedging and trees, providing privacy and an ideal outdoor space for family living and entertaining.\n\nInside, the property offers bright and generously proportioned accommodation throughout. The heart of the home is a magnificent open-plan kitchen, dining, and living space featuring impressive, vaulted ceilings which enhance the sense of space and light. This wonderful area is ideal for modern family living and entertaining, with large windows framing the surrounding gardens and bring the outdoors in.\n\nThe home offers spacious and versatile living accommodation, with well-proportioned bedrooms and excellent storage throughout, including 3 extra first floor habitle spaces making it an ideal choice for families seeking space, comfort, and a peaceful setting while remaining close to local amenities.\n\nLocation is a key feature of this property. Situated in the charming village of Glenealy, the home is within walking distance of the village shop, national school, local bar, forestry walks, and regular bus service. The property is also ideally located just 8 minutes from Exit 16 of the M11 motorway, providing easy access to Dublin and Wexford.\n\nThe towns of Rathdrum and Wicklow Town are both just 10 minutes away, offering a wide range of amenities including supermarkets, restaurants, schools, sports clubs, and train services.\n\nThis is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a spacious family home in a highly desirable village setting, surrounded by the natural beauty of County Wicklow while still enjoying excellent connectivity.\n\nViewings are highly recommended and are strictly by appointment only!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 10.7m x 2.79m: - \nWelcoming tiled entrance hallway leading to the main living accommodation. A secondary hallway with laminate flooring leads to the bedroom area. Shelved hot press with additional storage and shoe rack.\n\nLiving Room - 4.84m x 4.84m: - \nThe living room is a bright and spacious space featuring a striking vaulted ceiling and dual aspect windows overlooking the front and side gardens, allowing an abundance of natural light. The room benefits from wood flooring, wall lighting, feature brick wall and a multi-fuel stove which creates a warm focal point. A spiral staircase leads to the upstairs level.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 6.6m x 5.34m: - \nThe kitchen boasts a great range of solid oak fitted units at floor and eye level, complete with breakfast counter, shelving and wine rack. Integrated double oven, ceramic hob, fridge freezer, dishwasher and extractor hood. Solid wooden flooring and ceiling spotlights.The adjoining dining area benefits from a feature corner window allowing plenty of natural light, along with an open fireplace with brick surround and hearth. Wooden flooring with a tiled lower split-level area and double doors opening directly onto the gardens, creating an ideal space for family dining and entertaining.\n\nUtility Room - 3.76m x 1.73m: - \nWell-appointed utility room with fitted units at floor and eye level, ample countertop space with sink, mosaic tile splashback and tiled flooring. Plumbed for washing machine and dryer and housing the central heating burner. Door providing access to the garden and patio area.\n\nBedroom One - 3.94m x 2.97m: - \nSpacious double bedroom overlooking the front garden with laminate wood flooring and Velux window.\n\nWalk-in Wardrobe - 2.17m x 1.77m: - \nGenerous walk-in wardrobe with floor-to-ceiling storage, shelving, pull-out drawers, hanging rails and large wall mirror.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.17m x 2.08m: - \nThe ensuite bathroom comprises a bath with telephone-style mixer taps, WC, and WHB with tiling to the floor and partially tiled walls.\n\nBedroom two - 3.94m x 2.70m: - \nSpacious double room with built-in wardrobes and laminate wood flooring.\n\nBedroom three - 5.12m x 3.53m: - \nFeatures solid wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes, and dual aspect windows overlooking the patio area and rear garden.\n\nFirst Floor: - \n\n\nFamily Bathroom - 3.94m x 2.55m: - \nFully fitted with corner shower incorporating Mira pumped shower, corner bath, WC and WHB. Tiled flooring with tiled walls within the shower area.\n\nOpen Plan Area - 7.37m x 3.57m - \nA spiral staircase leads to a bright and spacious upper-level area overlooking the living room below. This impressive space features exposed timber beams and a timber ceiling, with two Velux windows providing lovely views of the surrounding fields and hills. Double doors open onto a wooden balcony with steps leading down to the gardens. Laminate flooring, ceiling spotlights and wall lights. Suitable space for a variety of uses such as home office, hobby / play rooms etc.\n\nRoom One - 6.02 x 3.35m: - \nVersatile room with laminate flooring, exposed timber beam, Velux window and excellent storage. TV and phone points.\n\nRoom Two - 5.11m x 2.13m: - \nSpacious room with Velux window and laminate flooring. Door leading to a large floored attic area providing extensive eaves storage with electrical power.\n\nGardens: - \nThe property enjoys beautifully maintained gardens to both the front and rear, with mature hedging, trees, plants and shrubs creating a private and peaceful setting. Attractive stone pillars and double gates open onto a sweeping gravel driveway providing ample parking and access around the property. The generous grounds provide excellent space for outdoor entertaining and offer potential for a garage or home office (subject to the usual planning permission). Outside tap and external power supply. The property also benefits from wonderful views of Carrick Mountain to the front and rolling countryside to the rear.Overall, this property offers spacious and flexible living accommodation in a peaceful setting with beautiful countryside views.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious detached home extending to approx. 225.9sq. m.</li><li> Set on a c. 0.5-acre landscaped site with views of Carrig Mountain to the front and Countryside views to the rear.</li><li> Gated entrance with sweeping gravel driveway, mature hedging, trees, plants and shrubs creating a private and peaceful setting.</li><li> Bright, spacious and flexible accommodation throughout.</li><li> Open-plan kitchen / dining and living area with vaulted ceilings up to open-plan gallery creating a wonderful sense of space.</li><li> Within walking distance to Glenealy village which offers local amenities, including national school, village shop, pub, bus service, forestry walks, sports facilities and outdoor recreation, while larger shopping, dining and train transport facilities are available in Wicklow Town.</li><li> c. 8 minutes to M11 (Exit 16) providing easy access to Dublin and Wexford.</li><li> A short drive brings you to a range of other wonderful amenities and attractions including the beautiful woodland walks of Avondale Forest Park, the stunning gardens at Kilmacurragh National Botanic Gardens, and the renowned sandy beaches of Brittas Bay.</ul>"
      },
